<title>LATVIA: Latvian Jan-Aug trade deficit soars.</title>
<headline>Latvian Jan-Aug trade deficit soars.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's trade deficit in the first eight months of the year grew by 14.7 percent versus the January to July period and by 86.7 percent compared with the first eight months of 1995, statistics department data showed on Friday.</p>
<p>All figures are in millions of lats, in real prices.</p>
<p> LATVIAN TRADE Jan-Aug '96    Jan-July '96    Jan-Aug '95</p>
<p> Exports	  509.19	   441.48	    437.43</p>
<p> Imports	  786.74	   683.51	    586.08</p>
<p> Deficit	  277.55	   242.03	    148.64</p>
<p>Largest export destination as percentage of total exports versus percentage in same period previous year:</p>
<p>Russia  - 23.6 (25.0)</p>
<p>Germany - 14.0 (14.3)</p>
<p>Britain - 10.7 (10.3)</p>
<p>Largest source of imports as percentage of total imports versus same period last year:</p>
<p>Russia  - 19.3 (21.0)</p>
<p>Germany - 14.0 (15.8)</p>
<p>Finland -  9.5 (11.0)</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
